{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "550da439-2137-8d3f-922b-e14b9fdf550e",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T11:04:06-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Gloria Ortiz",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sandra Pimentel",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:00:47-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, this is Sandra. Good morning, how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:00:52-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello? Oh, good morning. Can you hear me okay? I'm on the speakerphone, I'm sorry, my hands aren't so good with the phone."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:00:59-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you fine, hon. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:02-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I'm sorry to bother you. My name is Gloria Ortiz. I'm not sure I even have the right office. I'm trying to find out about a license, an entertainment license, for a bar that has live music."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:14-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You've got the right place. The clerk's office handles those. Are you looking to get one for a bar?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:20-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's not my bar. My nephew's friend has the bar, and he asked me to call, because I used to do the paperwork at, um, a different job. But now I don't know if it's the same thing. Is the entertainment license for the music, or for the bar? Because he already has a license for the drinks, I think."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:38-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Those are two separate things. The liquor license is one, and the entertainment license covers having live music or performers in the place. So he'd need that on top."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:47-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. On top. So it's two. Okay. And does it matter if it's only a guitar, one person, on Fridays? Or is that too small?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:01:55-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally even one performer counts as entertainment. I'd have him come in or call and we'll go over the application with him. Does he have the business name and the address handy?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:05-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't have those, I'm sorry. I only wrote down what he said. Should I have asked him first? I feel like I'm doing this wrong."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:13-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, you're fine. This is a good start. Now, he'll just want to have those details when he applies."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:20-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. Oh, and while I have you, I have another thing. It's for my dog. The license, the dog license. Do you do that too?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:28-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We do. Dog licenses go through us."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:31-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Because they want the rabies certificate, right? And I can't find the paper one. I have a copy from the vet, they printed it again. Is a copy accepted? Or does it have to be the, the original one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:43-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A copy from the vet is usually fine, as long as it's readable and shows the vaccine dates and the vet's information. If the vet printed you a new one, that's even better."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:02:53-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the copy is okay. Not the original. You're sure? I don't want to come down there and have them send me away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:00-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bring the copy and you should be all set. Is this for a new dog?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:05-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, he's six. I just never did it, well, my son always did it, and now I'm doing it. We have three generations in one house, me, my son and his wife, and the kids, so everybody thought somebody else did it. [pause] Is that bad? That it wasn't done?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:20-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, you'd be surprised how often that happens in a busy house. Just get it taken care of. Come on in when you can, or I can have the form ready for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:30-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, to say it back, I bring the vet copy for the dog. And my nephew's friend calls about the music license, the second one, separate from the drinks. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:41-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it exactly. Do you want me to take a number in case someone has questions?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:47-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, yes, please. It's 401-555-0193."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:49-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0193. Anything else I can help with, Gloria?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:53-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I think that's it. Thank you for being patient. I'm sorry I was so mixed up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:03:59-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You weren't a bit. Have a good day, and enjoy the rest of your morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:04:04-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye-bye now."
    }
  ],
